# Pin LF in the working tree, not just the index.
#
# memo writes its generated rule files with newline="\n" on every platform
# (see _apply in memo/cli.py) so that re-running `memo init` on Windows does
# not surface as a diff for teammates on Linux. With core.autocrlf=true the
# working tree would be smudged to CRLF on checkout and init's LF output
# would then rewrite every managed block. eol=lf keeps both sides LF
# regardless of each developer's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
